{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790960929,"nonce":"nqZBXQHmh1kzzS0YKfHE7JpSqTU=","title":"Embedders cannot learn that a call raised: no TieredRuntime API reads or clears the error-flag global","message":"A host calling a frontend function through its call cell gets the function's return value only; when the function raised, the error stays in the frontend's error-flag global (Python's py$exc) and the host sees a default value (0.0 for a float). TieredRuntime::set_error_flag_global names the global but nothing lets the host read or clear it.\n\nAdd a language-neutral TieredRuntime call that takes the pending error: returns the error-flag global's value and stores null. The host checks it after each host-to-Zyntax call, raises it in its own language, and keeps the object so it re-raises as itself if it comes back. No frontend names in zyntax_embed: the runtime knows only the global set by set_error_flag_global. Related: 70ab6405110e154dd3456a0a09a84dfb5a41e733218cbcac709e4ee33eafef48 (pending-exception model). Reported by caribou.","files":null}]}